 8. 🧀 1 for the road: Brew Crew parade today 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Images: Milwaukee Journal Sentinel Milwaukee Public Schools will close today for the Brewers' World Series Parade of Champions and Championship Rally, "Won Our Way."

 The Milwaukee Journal Sentinel says : "The Brewers are coming! Warm the buses! Clear the streets! Tap the kegs!" 🍻 Wisconsin Gov. Tony Evers (D) proclaimed today a statewide "Won Our Way" Day, honoring the Brewers and manager Pat Murphy for being "extraordinary players and people both on and off the field."

 Proclamation ... Parade map . Photo: Kevin Sabitus/Getty Images Above: Milwaukee Brewers pitcher Brandon Woodruff hoists the World Series trophy during the second quarter of last night's Green Bay Packers game at Lambeau Field. The Pack tamed the Carolina Panthers, 27-19. 

 Photo: Carmen Mandato/Getty Images This image, captured using a remote camera positioned above the diamond, shows Brewers catcher William Contreras celebrating after beating the Tampa Bay Rays in Game 5 in St. Petersburg, Fla., on Wednesday night.

 
 
